Only `lib` and `test` have an owner at 50% or more. `.github` and the root files have none.

I counted surviving lines with `git blame`, not the busfactor script's decayed commit weights, because you asked for lines. Details:
- **Ignored commits:** `62628c0` (the Fiona Formatter reformat) was skipped with `--ignore-rev`, so the lines it touched go to whoever wrote them before. I also used `-w -M -C` to follow moves and whitespace changes.
- **Bots:** I left out `dependabot[bot]` lines.
- **One person, one count:** Troy Goode's two emails (`<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example`) are merged. Alejandro Caravaca Puchades and `alex94puchades` share one email, so I merged those too.
- **Two commits kept:** I kept `b2005d9` (lib annotations) and `02afce3` (test coverage). They change content and are not formatting-only.
- **Binary files and lockfiles:** I excluded these from the count.

| Zone | Top holder | Share of surviving lines | Next |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/` | Troy Goode | 159/238 = 66.8% | Douglas Christopher Wilson 9.2% |
| `test/` | Troy Goode | 517/966 = 53.5% | Douglas Christopher Wilson 38.7% |
| `.github/` | none | top is Douglas Christopher Wilson, 118/366 = 32.2% | Íñigo Marquínez Prado 26.0%, Sebastian Beltran 17.2% |
| root files | none | top is Troy Goode, 134/415 = 32.3% | Douglas Christopher Wilson 27.7%, Jon Church 17.3% |

